Subject: [PATCH] generic-pc: guard channel-list input without local services

Generic-PC may have no local DVB services while still providing web radio,
IPTV or other GUI functionality.  In that state the common input handler can
receive KEY_OK before a bouquet list exists.  Treat it as an unavailable
channel-list action instead of dereferencing a null pointer.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform capability boundary]

--- a/src/neutrino.cpp
+++ b/src/neutrino.cpp
@@ -2949,5 +2949,10 @@ int CNeutrinoApp::showChannelList(const neutrino_msg_t _msg, bool from_menu)
 	}
 	channelList_painted = true;
 
+#if defined(HAVE_GENERIC_HARDWARE)
+	if (!bouquetList)
+		return menu_return::RETURN_NONE;
+#endif
+
 	neutrino_msg_t msg = _msg;
 	InfoClock->enableInfoClock(false);//TODO: use callback in channel list class
